        "position": { "x": 0, "y": 10 },
        "params": {
          "text": "THROAT SINGER\n\nDiphonic / overtone singing simulation with parallel formants.\n\nSignal:\n  Spectral Swarm (24 partials, formant 1200Hz) splits 3 ways:\n  → Choir A (vowel A) → VCA A ─┐\n  → Choir O (vowel O) → VCA B ─├→ Mixer → Wavefolder → Reverb → Compressor → Output\n  → Ring-Mod (× Sine Osc) → VCA C (25%) ─┘\n\n- Spectral Swarm: 24 partials, formantFreq=1200, formantQ=8, oddEven=-0.4\n- Two Choir modules in parallel with different vowels (A and O)\n- Ring-Mod adds metallic harmonic overtones (mixed subtly at 25%)\n- Wavefolder adds harmonic complexity\n- Compressor glues the mix together\n\nPlay LOW notes (C2-C3) for the best throat singing effect.\nSlow LFO modulates Choir A vowel; Chaos X modulates Choir O."
        }
      }
